<!DOCTYPE node PUBLIC "-//freedesktop//DTD D-BUS Object Introspection 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/dbus/1.0/introspect.dtd">
<!--
  The firewall members of io.kdos.Power1, kdos-powerd's face on the system
  bus, at /io/kdos/Power1 (src/daemons/kdos-powerd/bus.c). This is what the
  Firewall settings page and kdos-fwask call, and what their tests serve
  from a fake. The interface has other members (SetAccent, SetSplash, Accent,
  Accents) that neither program uses.

  NAMES, NEVER PORTS. A name is a row of kdos-powerd's own table; a name the
  table does not carry is refused with io.kdos.Power1.Error.NoSuchService,
  and nothing here can name a port.
-->
<node>
  <interface name="io.kdos.Power1">
    <!--
      One struct per row of the table, in its order: the name, whether it is
      open, and what it is for. Answered to anyone; it is the list
      `kdos-power firewall list` prints.
    -->
    <method name="ListFirewallServices">
      <arg name="services" type="a(sbs)" direction="out"/>
    </method>
    <!--
      Open or close one named service. polkit io.kdos.firewall.set, with
      interactive authorisation honoured: the caller sets the
      ALLOW_INTERACTIVE_AUTHORIZATION flag and polkit's agent asks for the
      password. Errors: org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.AccessDenied when polkit
      refuses, cannot be asked or the prompt is dismissed,
      org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.InteractiveAuthorizationRequired when the
      caller left the flag unset and a password would have been accepted,
      io.kdos.Power1.Error.NoSuchService before polkit is asked,
      io.kdos.Power1.Error.Failed with the daemon's own reason as its message.
    -->
    <method name="SetFirewallService">
      <arg name="name" type="s" direction="in"/>
      <arg name="open" type="b" direction="in"/>
    </method>
    <!--
      For each CLOSED service, in the table's order, the packets its knock
      counter has turned away since the ruleset was last loaded. Answered to
      anyone, with no polkit question: the counts say only that something
      knocked. A reload (every change is one) starts each counter again from
      zero. Counters the kernel could not be asked about are
      io.kdos.Power1.Error.Failed, and a daemon without them answers
      org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.UnknownMethod; both clients then carry on
      without counts.
    -->
    <method name="ListFirewallKnocks">
      <arg name="knocks" type="a(st)" direction="out"/>
    </method>
    <!--
      After a change is applied, over D-Bus or over the socket. It names no
      service: a listener asks ListFirewallServices again.
    -->
    <signal name="FirewallServicesChanged"/>
  </interface>
</node>
